      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61287090513e403cf345a5dd|full_name}: They plan to add it, but other than a mention that they will add it in [their docs](https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/vrc_oscbuttonin) I haven't seen anything recently. I have seen worlds make use of the fact that they can write to logs, and applications watching the logs closely. Well, \"Idle Home\" claims to write save data to logs every 10 mins (haven't checked yet, but no reason to disbelieve) and a world dedicated to showing off like booth models has a helper program that watches the logs for a specially crafted message with a URL so it can open up web pages if desired. \n\nI don't see VRChat letting udon directly talk to serial ports real or virtual, so you'd need a helper program anyways to take data from VRChat and send it to the daw anyways...",
